+## Live vs staged classification (FEAT-P2-001)
+
+Single authoritative live-vs-staged map. `compose/mct/` is **first-party** (adopted): the
+consolidated services are digest-pinned and in the pin/SBOM scope that `ci/validate.py`
+enforces for `compose/**` with `pins/images.lock`. The imported snapshot under
+**`mct/compose/` is archive-only** (vendored; not a deployment source — `mct/VENDORING.md`
+P3/P4), so no first-party deployment artifact may reference it. A cheap static guard asserts
+both boundaries (`automation/validation/tests/remediation_guards_test.sh`).
+
+| Service(s) | Classification | Path | Pin/SBOM scope |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| DFIR-IRIS, OpenCanary | Live — first-party, adopted | `compose/mct/` | yes (`compose/**` pin check + `pins/images.lock`) |
+| Shuffle, MISP, Velociraptor, OTel | Staged — archive-only | `mct/compose/` | no (must be pinned before revival) |
+| Greenbone, Security Onion | On their own VMs (preserved) | `mct/compose/` | no |
+
+The subtree fate (keep vs extract) and the archive-only enforcement approach are still the
+owner's decision (`docs/OWNER_DECISION_PACKAGE_2026-10-02.md` E-2a/E-2b); this
+classification does not preempt it.
+
